+## Pitfalls
+
+1. **Guessing parameter names** — Training data is wrong for TD 2025.32. Always call `td_get_par_info` for the operator type FIRST before setting any parameter.
+
+2. **`tdAttributeError` on script continue** — If `tdAttributeError` fires, STOP immediately. Call `td_get_operator_info` on the failing node before continuing. Scripting past the error corrupts the network state.
+
+3. **Hardcoded absolute paths in callbacks** — Using absolute paths in `scriptOp` callbacks breaks when the project moves. Always use `me.parent()` / `scriptOp.parent()` for relative references.
+
+4. **Destroy and recreate in same script** — Destroying and recreating same-named nodes in one `td_execute_python` call causes "Invalid OP object" errors. Split cleanup and creation into SEPARATE MCP calls.
+
+5. **`uTDCurrentTime` in GLSL TOP** — `uTDCurrentTime` does not exist in GLSL TOP uniforms. Use the Values page (`value0name = "uTime"`) and set expressions via `td_set_operator_pars` or `td_execute_python`.
+
+6. **8-bit texture freezing shaders** — Using `rgba8` format in Constant TOP clamps GLSL uniforms to 0-1, freezing time-based shaders. Always use `rgba32float` for uniform inputs.
+
+7. **Feedback TOP wiring wrong** — Feedback TOP requires the `top` parameter reference, not a direct input wire. "Not enough sources" resolves after first cook; "Cook dependency loop" warning is expected and harmless.
+
+8. **Non-Commercial codec restrictions** — H.264/H.265/AV1 require a Commercial TD license. On Non-Commercial, use `prores` (macOS) or `mjpa` as fallback, and cap resolution at 1280×1280.
+
+9. **Lag/Filter CHOP on spectrum data** — Lag CHOP and Filter CHOP expand AudioSpectrum output from 256 samples to 2400+ in timeslice mode, averaging to near-zero. Do NOT use them for spectrum smoothing — do it in GLSL.
+
+10. **AudioSpectrum timeslice OFF** — Turning TimeSlice OFF on AudioSpectrum processes the entire audio file at once (22050+ samples), causing CHOP-to-TOP overflow and killing the reactive pipeline.
+
+11. **Missing `outlength` on AudioSpectrum** — Default AudioSpectrum outputs 22050 samples. Always set `outputmenu='setmanually'` and `outlength=256` before connecting to CHOP-to-TOP.
+
+12. **Vertex access with `.x/.y/.z`** — In TD 2025.32 GLSL/SOP, vertex positions use `point.P[0]`, `point.P[1]`, `point.P[2]` — NOT `.x`, `.y`, `.z`. Using the dot syntax silently returns wrong values.
